implementationPlan.description:
The fix, test side only (governor comment-c35a995f: no scripts/moe-agent.* edit, no logs/ rewrite; the wrapper side is task-cd3887fe). In each of scripts/tests/prompt-cache.test.mjs, scripts/tests/prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs and scripts/tests/onboarding.mjs, right after the import block and BEFORE any test() registration or child process (mem:gotcha-node-test-top-level-await-ends-root-early: a selected test can start while later module statements still evaluate), add:
  // The launcher exports the seat's live usage receipt to every child; this file's fixture provider streams must never append to it (task-03418dc2).
  delete process.env.MOE_USAGE_RECEIPT_FILE;
  delete process.env.MOE_USAGE_CONTEXT_JSON;
Module top level runs before node:test starts any registered test and before onboarding.mjs's bundle-mode codex-stream at :52, so every spawn in each file, present or future, inherits a clean environment: prompt-cache.test.mjs :75/:86/:95 pass no env, prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs :366-368 spreads process.env, onboarding.mjs :52 passes none. Remove only these two keys; onboarding.mjs:65 already strips every MOE_* key for the daemon and proxy and stays as it is. Deleting an absent key is a no-op, so the files behave the same with or without the variables set; no other error handling is needed. Re-run the checkRefs command: G1 and the hunt repro now pass.
